          "message": "Add python_interpreter attr to pip rules (#252)\n\nThis adds a `python_interpreter` attribute to `pip_import` and `whl_library` that can be used to select the system command used to run Python's packaging tools. This provides the basis for invoking pip under Python 3 to install PY3 dependencies.\r\n\r\nExample usage:\r\n```\r\npip_import(\r\n    name = 'pip_deps',\r\n    requirements = '//:requirements.txt',\r\n    python_interpreter = 'python3.7',\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe par files have been regenerated. (This required a little bootstrapping since piptool.py needs to be modified to accept the flag before pip.bzl is modified to pass it.)",
          "tree": {
            "sha": "4d6d7ef1042fa4235bb962e9fcbf4d005041eaf3",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/rules_python/git/trees/4d6d7ef1042fa4235bb962e9fcbf4d005041eaf3"
          },
          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/rules_python/git/commits/7b222cfdb4e59b9fd2a609e1fbb233e94fdcde7c",
          "comment_count": 0,
          "verification": {
            "verified": true,
            "reason": "valid",
            "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsBcBAABCAAQBQJdyZsgCRBK7hj4Ov3rIwAAdHIIAHwg+zmWw91ZImRZhoFmpnYk\ni7Eg8YA40fpGMbpmwvEr4C85H/czBAJmLQzT6JzxvRtzDltomML/5X6ZQcJXpgvJ\nyV+Cu+C5L/LXQfQk9d4xKZpUcFoIT0xXtEDrFCoOcm5x35KBepQ+fgNNabn5VVti\nlLLoU6CFj1USggWY+2AaFKUsWwHIA+bVfxgPsv434Zbb+hbuLBvoZjMQyx8eqbtW\naiIygnKxTbHeyQkgca+1SMTkS/NuEEMgpTfn4ES6KRrBXHetxW5AlOe/5DKqfkTC\nN/qOJL3q4+OBxvTMW2nv/sxybELNnllQV8jcscFNPbKbE50MDd7GrIXP1xMbkPk=\n=xu8X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
            "payload": "tree 4d6d7ef1042fa4235bb962e9fcbf4d005041eaf3\nparent 13bf8b7769c5eeabdda5d9ea0cf3ae9e895cc61c\nauthor Jon Brandvein <brandjon@google.com> 1573493536 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1573493536 -0500\n\nAdd python_interpreter attr to pip rules (#252)\n\nThis adds a `python_interpreter` attribute to `pip_import` and `whl_library` that can be used to select the system command used to run Python's packaging tools. This provides the basis for invoking pip under Python 3 to install PY3 dependencies.\r\n\r\nExample usage:\r\n```\r\npip_import(\r\n    name = 'pip_deps',\r\n    requirements = '//:requirements.txt',\r\n    python_interpreter = 'python3.7',\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe par files have been regenerated. (This required a little bootstrapping since piptool.py needs to be modified to accept the flag before pip.bzl is modified to pass it.)"
